## This port

The files in `upstream/lxx74-cups-0.8.2-z33/` are byte-for-byte the
2005 release; the pristine tree is also git-tagged
`lxx74-cups-0.8.2-z33-original` (the first commit of the history), so
`git diff lxx74-cups-0.8.2-z33-original..main` shows every change
made by this port. `src/rastertolxz33.c` is derived from it with the
following functional changes (same license, GPL v2):

- CUPS raster page-header reading rewritten to support all raster
  versions produced by current CUPS/Ghostscript pipelines (v1 `RaSt`,
  v2 `RaS2`, and the modern v3 `RaS3` format in which the sync word is
  stored outside the header struct), including byte-order handling.
- Filter argument parsing fixed to the CUPS convention
  (`argv[5]=copies argv[6]=options argv[7]=filename`); the original
  misparsed real CUPS invocations.
- 64-bit portability fixes (pointer/integer casts, format strings).
- End-of-stream handling: the page loop now ends cleanly when the
  raster input ends instead of exiting with an error.
- Version banner emitted to the CUPS debug log.

Security hardening added in this port:

- Strict validation of the raster page header (width/height/resolution
  bounds, exact cupsWidth/cupsBitsPerPixel/cupsBytesPerLine
  consistency) before any buffer allocation or printer output,
  closing heap out-of-bounds read/write paths reachable from crafted
  raster headers.
- Fixed a per-page pixbuf leak; scan buffer, page header and device
  structures are now released on all exit paths (verified with
  LeakSanitizer).
- Build hardening: _FORTIFY_SOURCE=3, stack protector, PIE, full RELRO.
- Unknown CUPS job options are ignored quietly instead of raising
  job-level errors.

The printer initialisation blob (`z33-preamble.bin`) is unchanged from
the 2005 release.
